Hello,

I have a novice question (I think) regarding the use of dynamic input values in shiny.

In the online examples...it shows the basic framework for shiny operation as...input values => R code => output values.

I would like to know if it is possible to do the following...R code => input values => R code => output values

I will need to run an r script to query a database for possible values I would like to supply to a user selectable field in the shiny app. I do not know what these values will be ahead of time. Based on what the user selects from the list...that would then feed into the second R code evaluation and dictate the output.

Can somethign like this be done? Any pointers on where to start?

