Yes, I'd create an HTML based menu (frameset or iframe based?) that displays the apps. To host the apps themselves you have the following options:
The second argument to runApp is indeed port number. So yes, you could start 15 apps on different ports if you wanted to. You probably then also want to pass the "launch.browser=FALSE" argument so 15 browsers don't spawn!
The glimmer.rstudio.com <http://glimmer.rstudio.com> server that you pointed to is available for public beta testing (it's free during beta testing but is likely to become a paid service at some point). You can register by going to http://rstudio.com/shiny/ and clicking the "register now" link near the bottom.
In late January we'll be releasing the software that runs on glimmer.rstudio.com <http://glimmer.rstudio.com> for beta testing, so you can run it on your own server (Linux required, for the first version at least).
Hope that helps.

